  "says": "Mr. Saxena, I have paid the amounts you specified. Regarding the balance of two hundred and seventy rupees: I am not a public servant, nor am I in contract with the state in the sense of §294. I am a resident in a bungalow allotted to me, albeit by a clerical error. To recover my personal expenditure from the state's imprest is a confusion of categories. I will settle this debt directly with the Directorate, but I ask that it not be treated as a defalcation from the treasury.",
  "thought": "The payment was mechanical, a series of subtractions that left me lighter in pocket but no lighter in spirit. Saxena’s indifference is the friction of the universal against the particular; he sees a file, I see a man, and the system mediates the contradiction by making me pay for the privilege of existing here. My stomach growls, a reminder that the ethical idea does not fill one’s belly, and the heat is pressing in despite the shade.",
